{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config/settings.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:01:13.452156Z","id":"ccdd72378bd22d59ec79e17e20f163686ba15f7b3e842927f6bec2d8156d2733","body":{"detail":"settings::write holds the process-wide WRITING mutex across its read, edit and rename, but crates/clax-commands/src/plugin_bin.rs (clax bin set / clear) rewrites the same file from the CLI process with no lock shared with the daemon. Both replace the whole file, so whichever renames last drops the other's edit. No file lock or compare-on-rename (re-read and compare the text before rename) guards it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":167},"end":{"line":169},"content_hash":"aea54350b20169a1d6b5fb36a1d4041c4c3dd42bae78c5bae23d9c460209af2d"},"suggested_fix":"Take an advisory lock on <home>/config.toml.lock in both writers, or re-read the file just before the rename and retry when it changed.","summary":"config.toml writes are serialized only within one process: clax bin set and a daemon's PUT /api/settings can lose each other's change","tags":["config","claxbot","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config/settings.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:01:13.452276Z","id":"6e4ee4c47b87073cde2ea4a6115e73105d9bb8d5bd7fdc30a9ec37ef4eb83ecb","body":{"detail":"Every reader (Sampler::from_home, the journal's start, terminal_after_s, the port) reads its table once when the daemon starts, so LIVE_KEYS is empty and every PUT /api/settings answers restart_required: true while the daemon keeps its old values. Reloading [sample] or [bot] in place would need their holders (AppState.sample) to be swappable.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":57},"content_hash":"7346d6553110ce66178f62182d552d24f59388a93df1cc26ed485610dca179f5"},"summary":"Apply a written setting to the running daemon instead of reporting restart_required","tags":["revisit:a reader reads its table per use (ClaxBot reading [bot] per run), or the settings screen needs changes without a restart","claxbot","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config/settings.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:19:49.440023Z","id":"6aab7c824e9a0948f805001c7a25e301573507f144e50b2fbc52254f33f28959","body":{"detail":"settings::write holds the process-wide WRITING mutex across its read, edit and rename, but crates/clax-commands/src/plugin_bin.rs (clax bin set / clear) rewrites the same file from the CLI process with no lock shared with the daemon. Both replace the whole file, so whichever renames last drops the other's edit. No file lock or compare-on-rename (re-read and compare the text before rename) guards it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":200},"end":{"line":202},"content_hash":"aea54350b20169a1d6b5fb36a1d4041c4c3dd42bae78c5bae23d9c460209af2d"},"suggested_fix":"Take an advisory lock on <home>/config.toml.lock in both writers, or re-read the file just before the rename and retry when it changed.","summary":"config.toml writes are serialized only within one process: clax bin set and a daemon's PUT /api/settings can lose each other's change","supersedes":"ccdd72378bd22d59ec79e17e20f163686ba15f7b3e842927f6bec2d8156d2733","tags":["config","claxbot","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config/settings.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:19:49.457304Z","id":"21641a9bc578723be0b93f5e6d21295ddec9b185140a0789fae034abb89f9d78","body":{"detail":"Every reader (Sampler::from_home, the journal's start, terminal_after_s, the port) reads its table once when the daemon starts, so LIVE_KEYS is empty and every PUT /api/settings answers restart_required: true; GET shows the new value as `pending` beside the value in effect (AppState.settings.running). Reloading [sample] or [bot] in place would need their holders (AppState.sample) to be swappable.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":79},"content_hash":"55076ae439290dcb3a8abf67292b6a938743319b1f6f18eb4dc90413f887c582"},"summary":"Apply a written setting to the running daemon instead of reporting restart_required","supersedes":"6e4ee4c47b87073cde2ea4a6115e73105d9bb8d5bd7fdc30a9ec37ef4eb83ecb","tags":["revisit:a reader reads its table per use (ClaxBot reading [bot] per run), or the settings screen needs changes without a restart","claxbot","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config/settings.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:30:08.432118Z","id":"090088b476999e73d8cdb5c12ca215c6b92ceca2c89f7e29a948d82c8aac6521","body":{"detail":"settings::write holds the process-wide WRITING mutex across its read, edit and rename, but crates/clax-commands/src/plugin_bin.rs (clax bin set / clear) reads and rewrites the same file from the CLI process (through the same settings::write_file) with no lock shared with the daemon. Both replace the whole file, so whichever renames last drops the other's edit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":206},"end":{"line":208},"content_hash":"aea54350b20169a1d6b5fb36a1d4041c4c3dd42bae78c5bae23d9c460209af2d"},"suggested_fix":"Take an advisory lock on <home>/config.toml.lock in both writers, or re-read the file just before the rename and retry when it changed.","summary":"config.toml writes are serialized only within one process: clax bin set and a daemon's PUT /api/settings can lose each other's change","supersedes":"6aab7c824e9a0948f805001c7a25e301573507f144e50b2fbc52254f33f28959","tags":["config","claxbot","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config/settings.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:30:08.451495Z","id":"c65f5562115e958b44e1e6cc07342c8dc74329e91cc64e6c00196484365cd310","body":{"detail":"Every reader (Sampler::from_home, the journal's start, terminal_after_s, the port) reads its table once when the daemon starts, so LIVE_KEYS is empty and every PUT /api/settings answers restart_required: true; GET shows the new value as `pending` beside the value in effect (AppState.settings.running). Reloading [sample] or [bot] in place would need their holders (AppState.sample) to be swappable.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":81},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"55076ae439290dcb3a8abf67292b6a938743319b1f6f18eb4dc90413f887c582"},"summary":"Apply a written setting to the running daemon instead of reporting restart_required","supersedes":"21641a9bc578723be0b93f5e6d21295ddec9b185140a0789fae034abb89f9d78","tags":["revisit:a reader reads its table per use (ClaxBot reading [bot] per run), or the settings screen needs changes without a restart","claxbot","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
